//anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#AnonymousNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property> _:d6c9bf45d32dacb738131c0fca5ccd50 .\n_:d6c9bf45d32dacb738131c0fca5ccd50 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message> \"AnonymousNode requires exactly one non-empty role.\" .\n_:d6c9bf45d32dacb738131c0fca5ccd50 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#minLength> \"1\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .\n_:d6c9bf45d32dacb738131c0fca5ccd50 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#datatype> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n_:d6c9bf45d32dacb738131c0fca5ccd50 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount> \"1\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .\n_:d6c9bf45d32dacb738131c0fca5ccd50 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#minCount> \"1\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .\n_:d6c9bf45d32dacb738131c0fca5ccd50 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#role> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#AnonymousNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Role presence and uri exclusion.\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#AnonymousNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Anonymous Node Shape\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#AnonymousNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#targetClass> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#AnonymousNode> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#AnonymousNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#NamedNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property> _:e5d31b8148d5c67a853c28ba0e53265 .\n_:e5d31b8148d5c67a853c28ba0e53265 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message> \"hasProp must point at a Prop.\" .\n_:e5d31b8148d5c67a853c28ba0e53265 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#class> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#Prop> .\n_:e5d31b8148d5c67a853c28ba0e53265 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#hasProp> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#NamedNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property> _:e7810b220c9a6a1a26c35bb0d81e1b1c .\n_:e7810b220c9a6a1a26c35bb0d81e1b1c <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message> \"NamedNode admits at most one projection.\" .\n_:e7810b220c9a6a1a26c35bb0d81e1b1c <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#class> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#Projection> .\n_:e7810b220c9a6a1a26c35bb0d81e1b1c <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount> \"1\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .\n_:e7810b220c9a6a1a26c35bb0d81e1b1c <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#hasProjection> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#NamedNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property> _:b207dec460fbf758d201a0ff25f54a90 .\n_:b207dec460fbf758d201a0ff25f54a90 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message> \"NamedNode must not have a role (use AnonymousNode instead).\" .\n_:b207dec460fbf758d201a0ff25f54a90 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount> \"0\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .\n_:b207dec460fbf758d201a0ff25f54a90 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#role> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#NamedNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property> _:bf90bb658d08d3402b47dea5e89c65b3 .\n_:bf90bb658d08d3402b47dea5e89c65b3 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message> \"URI must be dot-separated lowercase path or '$custom'.\" .\n_:bf90bb658d08d3402b47dea5e89c65b3 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#pattern> \"^(\\\\$custom|[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*(\\\\.[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*)*)$\" .\n_:bf90bb658d08d3402b47dea5e89c65b3 <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#uri> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#NamedNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property> _:fc2c088e64cb9325505a2d747850028a .\n_:fc2c088e64cb9325505a2d747850028a <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message> \"NamedNode requires exactly one non-empty uri.\" .\n_:fc2c088e64cb9325505a2d747850028a <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#minLength> \"1\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .\n_:fc2c088e64cb9325505a2d747850028a <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#datatype> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n_:fc2c088e64cb9325505a2d747850028a <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount> \"1\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .\n_:fc2c088e64cb9325505a2d747850028a <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#minCount> \"1\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .\n_:fc2c088e64cb9325505a2d747850028a <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#uri> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#NamedNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"URI encoding and presence constraints.\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#NamedNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Named Node Shape\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#NamedNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#targetClass> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#NamedNode> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#NamedNodeShape> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#SpecificationShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#property> _:bbd88179c965ce670295990179bca70c .\n_:bbd88179c965ce670295990179bca70c <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#message> \"Specification requires exactly one rootNode of type NamedNode.\" .\n_:bbd88179c965ce670295990179bca70c <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#class> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#NamedNode> .\n_:bbd88179c965ce670295990179bca70c <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount> \"1\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .\n_:bbd88179c965ce670295990179bca70c <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#minCount> \"1\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .\n_:bbd88179c965ce670295990179bca70c <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#rootNode> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#SpecificationShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Root document constraints.\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#SpecificationShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"Specification Shape\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#SpecificationShape> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#targetClass> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#Specification> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#SpecificationShape> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#NodeShape> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"documentationStages\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"summary\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"_meta.title\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Dot-delimited GraphQL field path relative to the enclosing data context. On a node: the field the node renders. On a relation: the traversal populating the slot. Names the field only, never an unwrapping path like edges/node — whether a plural field is a connection or a plain list is a provider mechanism discovered from the schema. The relation's cardinality maps onto the field's shape: upper bound to multiplicity, lower bound to nullability.\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#Projection> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"projection field\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionField> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"spinner\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"checkmark\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"chevron-down\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"The fixed value the anatomy pins the prop to.\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#Prop> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"prop value\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propValue> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"icon\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propName> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Name of the pinned prop, as defined on the referenced component in the design system ontology.\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#Prop> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"prop name\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#propName> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"Pattern\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"OntologyClass\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"Component\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"GraphQL type condition, like a Relay fragment's 'on'. On a root node it establishes the data context for the tree; on a child it narrows the traversed entity's type, like an inline fragment.\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#Projection> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"projection type\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#projectionType> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"selected\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"disabled\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"focus\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"active\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"hover\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Interaction state this style value applies in. Absent\\n    means the default state. Closed vocabulary (hover, active, focus,\\n    disabled, selected), governed by registry — 'active' subsumes Material's\\n    'pressed' and Spectrum's 'down'; 'focus' maps to CSS :focus-visible\\n    (Spectrum's 'key-focus'). States re-value style channels only: they never\\n    add structure (that is the Switch construct) and never define transitions\\n    or interaction logic (state machines stay out of scope). Authored as an\\n    @state suffix on the style key.\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#Style> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"style state\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleState> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"color/surface/button?\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"color/surface/primary\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"spacing/medium\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> \"stack\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> \"Value for a style property.\" .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#Style> .\n<http://anatomy-dsl.example.org/ontology#styleValue> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> \"style value\" .\n<http://an